    "notes": "Guard-gated, ultra-exclusive waterfront community in Coral Gables, FL 33156, developed in the early 1960s by ALCOA founder Arthur Vining Davis. Widely regarded as America's most expensive residential neighborhood. 192 single-family lots (166 waterfront) on over 200 acres of Biscayne Bay shoreline with engineered deep-water sea-walled canals, bridge-free bay access, and 24/7 guard. Entry price $10M+. Membership in Gables Estates Club, Inc. (with non-refundable six-figure application fee and resident sponsorship) is required before purchase."
